feat(phase5): server-side result guard for MCP tools

When the LLM asks about a specific identifier (B-sorszam, M-sorszam,
device, customer, j_szam, munkaszam) but the tool's response contains
hits for a DIFFERENT identifier, the LLM has been known to confabulate
— paraphrasing the wrong data as if it answered the question. The
M09192 -> M11357/M06079 case in Phase 5 was the visible symptom.

This adds a two-stage guard in mcp-server.ts that wraps the call() for
every search/lookup tool:

  1. extractIds(args) pulls identifiers out of the LLM-supplied
     tool args (explicit sorszam/device/customer fields, j_szam,
     munkaszam, OR sorszam-like patterns found in the free-text q).
  2. checkResult(ids, response, tool) walks the response and:
     - lets the raw response through if all asked ids are in some hit,
     - REPLACES the response with a canned "no match" message if the
       asked identifier is not in any hit (and there ARE results).
       The raw body is kept under `original` for debugging.

Stats/aggregations pass through unchanged (no per-hit identity to
check). Tool name is included in the canned message so the LLM can
decide what to retry.

The M09192 question: with this guard, the LLM's call to
search_serviz_belso with q="M09192" that returned a fuzzy
M11357/M06079 hit will now get back a canned response that says
"no record for M09192, closest match is M11357/M06079" instead of
the raw M11357 spec sheet.

Tests: 23 new cases in 20-result-guard.test.ts cover the matching
rules (sorszam / device / customer / m_sorszam / j_szam / munkaszam),
bidirectional customer matching, the M09192 scenario, the
English canned path, and the stats-aggregation skip.

Full suite: 324/324 pass (was 301), 1642 expects, tsc clean.
